From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: host: reset the xHCI after system sleep

A USB drive that stayed plugged into an SM8550 Retroid Pocket 6 across
system sleep (deep or s2idle) was gone after wake: the xHCI reported
"Host System Error" on resume, the drive stopped answering ("device not
accepting address", -108) and was disconnected. Without wakeup, dwc3
suspends the host with dwc3_core_exit(), which resets the controller,
but the xHCI then tried to restore its old state.

Give the dwc3 xHCI a new "xhci-reset-on-resume-quirk" property that
xhci-plat turns into XHCI_RESET_ON_RESUME, so the controller is
reinitialised and its devices are reset-resumed.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@
 
 int dwc3_host_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 {
-	struct property_entry	props[6];
+	struct property_entry	props[8];
 	struct platform_device	*xhci;
 	int			ret, irq;
 	int			prop_idx = 0;
@@ -167,6 +167,14 @@
 
 	props[prop_idx++] = PROPERTY_ENTRY_BOOL("write-64-hi-lo-quirk");
 
+	/*
+	 * System suspend without wakeup runs dwc3_core_exit(), which resets the
+	 * controller, so the xHCI has lost its state on resume. Restoring it
+	 * failed with "Host System Error" and dropped every device that stayed
+	 * plugged in (Retroid Pocket 6, SM8550); reinitialise it instead.
+	 */
+	props[prop_idx++] = PROPERTY_ENTRY_BOOL("xhci-reset-on-resume-quirk");
+
 	if (dwc->usb3_lpm_capable)
 		props[prop_idx++] = PROPERTY_ENTRY_BOOL("usb3-lpm-capable");
 
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
@@ -277,6 +277,9 @@
 		if (device_property_read_bool(tmpdev, "xhci-skip-phy-init-quirk"))
 			xhci->quirks |= XHCI_SKIP_PHY_INIT;
 
+		if (device_property_read_bool(tmpdev, "xhci-reset-on-resume-quirk"))
+			xhci->quirks |= XHCI_RESET_ON_RESUME;
+
 		device_property_read_u32(tmpdev, "imod-interval-ns",
 					 &xhci->imod_interval);
 		device_property_read_u16(tmpdev, "num-hc-interrupters",
